      "content": "A calibration error? That's a huge red flag for an auditor. If the scale was set wrong, how do we know the previous readings—and the ones we're seeing now—are actually accurate? \n\nI just opened that report you sent, and I'm looking at the \"corrected\" values you provided. They look a little too perfect, almost like they were manually adjusted to fit the spec. If I present this to the Board and they decide to do a spot check on the raw data logs versus your calibration report, and they see a discrepancy, it's going to look like we're hiding a structural defect.\n\nCan you show me the raw, uncorrected telemetry from the exact moment the reading was at 88%? I need to see the data *before* your calibration fix was applied so I can personally verify that this was just a scale issue and not a real tension drop. If the raw data shows a real dip in tension, I can't sign off on this.",
